# HYDRAX Mobile — environment template.
#
#   cp mobile/.env.example mobile/.env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. Expo reads it automatically at bundle time and
# substitutes any variable whose name starts with EXPO_PUBLIC_.
#
# IMPORTANT — what may go in this file:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are compiled INTO the app bundle. Anyone with the
#   .apk can read them. Never put HYDRAX_ADMIN_KEY, HYDRAX_DEVICE_KEY, a
#   database URL or any other secret here. The app is read-only and needs no
#   credentials at all — see docs/MOBILE.md, "Authentication".

# --- backend location --------------------------------------------------------
#
# Where the HYDRAX backend is reachable FROM THE PHONE.
#
# Leave this unset for normal development: when you run `npm start`, the app
# works out the backend address from the machine serving it (your laptop's LAN
# IP, port 8080). That is the right answer almost every time.
#
# Set it when:
#   - the backend runs on a different machine than Metro
#   - the backend runs on a different port
#   - you are building a standalone APK, which has no dev server to ask
#
# Use the laptop's LAN IP, never "localhost": on a phone, localhost is the
# phone. Find it with `ipconfig` on Windows (IPv4 Address) or `ip addr` on
# Linux/macOS.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8080

# Android emulator only — the emulator reaches the host machine at 10.0.2.2:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8080
